---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SpecCard from '../components/SpecCard.astro';

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  'headline': "Meta-ExternalAgent: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It | PromptDNS",
  'description': "Meta-ExternalAgent explained: what Meta's crawler does, its user-agent token, robots.txt behavior, how to verify it, and how to block or allow it.",
  'author': { '@type': 'Organization', 'name': 'PromptDNS', 'url': 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  'datePublished': '2026-10-28',
  'dateModified': '2026-10-28',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Does blocking Meta-ExternalAgent affect my Facebook page?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. The crawler collects web content for AI training; your Facebook page is a separate platform."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do I verify Meta-ExternalAgent?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Reverse DNS on the fetching IP should resolve to a Meta or Facebook address."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Is Meta-ExternalAgent the same as FacebookBot?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. FacebookBot is the older crawler for the assistant; Meta-ExternalAgent is the newer AI training crawler."}}],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Meta-ExternalAgent: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It | PromptDNS"
  description="Meta-ExternalAgent explained: what Meta's crawler does, its user-agent token, robots.txt behavior, how to verify it, and how to block or allow it."
  breadcrumb={[["Home", "/"], ["AI Web Infrastructure", "/ai-web-infrastructure/"], ["Meta-ExternalAgent"]]}
  schema={[articleSchema, faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Meta-ExternalAgent</span>
    </nav>
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">AI crawler</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Meta-ExternalAgent: User-Agent, robots.txt Rules and How to Verify It</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Meta-ExternalAgent is Meta's crawler that collects data for training and improving Meta AI models. It honors robots.txt, and Disallow: Meta-ExternalAgent keeps your content out of Meta AI training. Genuine fetches resolve to Meta-hosted addresses, which is how you verify them.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Crawler specification">
      <SpecCard
        name="Meta-ExternalAgent"
        operator="Meta"
        token="Meta-ExternalAgent"
        purpose="AI training and retrieval for Meta AI"
        robots="honors Disallow: Meta-ExternalAgent"
        verify="Reverse DNS resolves to *.meta.com or *.facebook.com"
        evidence="Documented"
        verified="2026-10-28"
        href="/ai-crawlers-list/"
      />
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>How to block Meta-ExternalAgent</h2>
      <p>Add this rule to your robots.txt at the root of your domain:</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">User-agent: Meta-ExternalAgent
Disallow: /</pre>
      <p>Blocking Meta-ExternalAgent removes your content from Meta AI training. FacebookBot is a separate crawler for the older chatbot use case.</p>

      <h2>How to allow Meta-ExternalAgent</h2>
      <p>Allowing Meta-ExternalAgent makes your content available to Meta AI answers and training.</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft mt-3">
User-agent: meta-externalagent
Allow: /
</pre>

      <h2>How to verify Meta-ExternalAgent</h2>
      <p>The reliable check is reverse DNS on the fetching IP address. Run the lookup below against any visitor claiming the Meta-ExternalAgent token; a genuine fetch resolves inside Meta's address space, and a spoofed one does not.</p>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft">dig +short -x 203.0.113.5  # e.g. for fetching-ip>
# A genuine Meta-ExternalAgent fetch resolves to an Meta address</pre>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The Meta-ExternalAgent decision is per vendor and reversible: robots.txt is a one-line edit, and the verification method tells you within seconds whether a visit was genuine. Revisit the decision quarterly as each vendor's product boundaries keep moving.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does blocking Meta-ExternalAgent affect my Facebook page?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. The crawler collects web content for AI training; your Facebook page is a separate platform.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify Meta-ExternalAgent?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Reverse DNS on the fetching IP should resolve to a Meta or Facebook address.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is Meta-ExternalAgent the same as FacebookBot?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. FacebookBot is the older crawler for the assistant; Meta-ExternalAgent is the newer AI training crawler.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Related:
        <a href="/ai-crawlers-list/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">all AI crawlers</a>,
        <a href="/ai-crawler-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">AI crawler checker</a>,
        <a href="/robots-txt-guide/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">robots.txt guide</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
